{title: Whispering Hope}
{artist: Septimus Winner}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: G}
{key_original: Db}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Soft as the voice of an angel
[D7]Breathing a lesson un[G]heard
[G]Hope with a gentle persuasion
[D7]Whispers her comforting [G]word
[G]Wait till the darkness is over
[C]Wait till the tempest is [G]done
[D7]Hope for the sunshine tomorrow
[D7]After the shower is [G]gone
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Whispering hope, oh how welcome thy voice
[D7]Making my heart in its sorrow re[G]joice
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]If in the dusk of the twilight
[D7]Dim be the region a[G]far
[G]Will not the deepening darkness
[D7]Brighten the glimmering [G]star
[G]Then when the night is upon us
[C]Why should the heart sink a[G]way
[G]When the dark midnight is over
[D7]Watch for the breaking of [G]day
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
